          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-30 04:06:14.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20565 tests: use EC_* layouts in sanity-ec 58b-65d",
        "message": "LU-20565 tests: use EC_* layouts in sanity-ec 58b-65d\n\nsanity-ec degraded-read subtests 58b-65d hard-coded an EC 4+2\nlayout with a gate of 6 or 8 OSTs, although the geometry did not\nmatter to what they tested.  They would be skipped on the 4 and 7\nOST test sessions.\n\nUse the EC_ARG, EC_DSTRIPE and EC_CSTRIPE defaults that enable_ec()\nscales to OSTCOUNT and drop the gates, so they run with 3 OSTs.\nScale sizes and offsets tied to a 4-stripe row to EC_DSTRIPE, and\nput each PFL boundary in front of an EC component on a multiple of\nthe row width.  60d and 65c mix a 2+1 component with the default\nlayout and need 4 OSTs so the two differ.  With only one parity\nstripe, 59a and 63c skip their two-OST part, and 58b, 61d and 65d,\nwhich only fail two OSTs, are skipped.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-ec\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-ec ostcount=4\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I8a0d5693af6204d29defa5da9fbb505a123ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
